First, we need to find out how many yogurts Terry eats in 30 days. He eats 2 yogurts per day, so in 30 days he eats 2 * 30 = 60 yogurts.

Next, we need to find out how many sets of 4 yogurts are in 60 yogurts.  60 / 4 = 15 sets.

Each set of 4 yogurts costs $5.00, so 15 sets cost 15 * $5.00 = $75.00.

Therefore, Terry spends $75.00 on yogurt over 30 days.

#### 75 [end of text]


